
The C interpreter includes the checked-in i*.c instruction sources by default.

To regenerate them without modifying the source tree, install CLISP and run
from the repository root:

    cmake -S . -B build -DVLM_REGENERATE_STUBS=ON
    cmake --build build --parallel

The generator writes the instruction sources into build/stub. CMake tracks
the assembler and Lisp macro dependencies and compiles those generated copies.
The generate-stubs target runs just the generation step.

Running "clisp -norc process.lisp" directly from this directory still overwrites
the checked-in copies. Set VLM_STUB_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY to an existing directory
with a trailing slash to select a different destination.
